//****************************************************************************
// $Module type: Class Package
// $Module name: cFTGridHost
// $Author     : Nils Svedmyr, RDC Tools International, <mailto:support@rdctools.com>
// Web-site    : http://www.rdctools.com
// Created     : 2026-09-28
//
// Description : A cFTLocalWebControlHost laid out on a grid of 8 px columns the way a Windows dialog is -
//               controls at their size, the extra space where the window stretches.
//
// This code is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY;
// without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
//****************************************************************************
Use cFTLocalWebControlHost.pkg

/* THE GRID HOST (Nils 2026-09-27: "we are really building a Windows application"). The columns are a FIXED
   8 px, so a control's piColumnSpan is its width in 8 px steps and piColumnIndex its place, much like dialog
   units - the same at any window size. It began as Demo-RDCFlexTron's prototype, cDemoGridHost.

   - peLayoutType ltGrid: a control sits in a column AND a row - piColumnIndex and piRowIndex, both counted
     from 0 - and piColumnSpan / piRowSpan say how many it takes.
   - psDefaultColumnWidth "8px": every column is 8 px unless psColumnWidths says otherwise.
   - psDefaultRowHeight: a row is as tall as its tallest control, and never less than one FT row (--ft-row
     in ftcontrols.css, 33 px: a button's 29 px box with its 2 px margins), so an empty row keeps the height
     of a row of buttons.

   THE COUNT. piColumnCount is the widest row's width in 8 px steps, plus the one column that stretches: the
   controls that stay at the left, 1, and the ones that stay at the right. Every column takes 8 px whether it
   is used or not, so the count follows the content - unused columns would be an empty strip at the right
   edge - and the host must be at least as wide as its fixed columns at the window's MINIMUM size. Rows count
   themselves: the framework counts them from the controls' piRowIndex.

   WHERE THE WINDOW STRETCHES is the object's to say: psColumnWidths "43/1fr" gives column 43 the extra width
   (an empty column between the left and right groups, or one under a field that grows); psRowHeights "1/1fr"
   gives row 1 the extra height (a page or a list, with pbFillHeight). Never percentages: they are a share of
   the WHOLE height and ignore the other rows. A width entry past piColumnCount is ignored.

   AIR between groups is a row of its own: an empty row of a fixed height, psRowHeights "3/8px" (one column's
   width), so a button row does not sit right under a list or a page. The theme puts no gap between rows -
   only each control's own margins, 2 px above and below, which leave 4 px: right between two rows of
   buttons, too little under a page.

   THE HOST'S OWN HEIGHT is its rows and 8 px more: the Web UI theme pads a host's content by 4 px above and
   below. A bar of one row of buttons needs 41 px - about 26 dialog units at 100 % - and one of two rows 74 px,
   about 48. A host shorter than its content scrolls, and shows a scroll bar at its right edge: the
   framework's page is a scroller. (A program can hide that bar in its own application.css instead, as
   DFRefactor does; the few pixels are then cut off.)

   The grid trap: piColumnSpan 0 means ONE column here, not "the rest of the row" as in the flow layout - a
   control that spans the width says how many columns. A caption longer than its span is cut off, as in a
   Windows dialog: size the control to its caption - or put a row of buttons in a cFTWebButtonRow, where each
   is as wide as its caption. The FT button's 76 px minimum steps aside on a grid host (ftcontrols.css), where
   the span is the width.

   The OverrideProperty tags tell the Studio these are the class's own defaults, so its Designer and property
   panel show them; the Sets make them so at run time. The last one, psCSSClass, is the host's own FtHost
   (cFTLocalWebControlHost.pkg), stated again as the two tags above it are. */
{ OverrideProperty=peLayoutType InitialValue=ltGrid }
{ OverrideProperty=psDefaultColumnWidth InitialValue="8px" }
{ OverrideProperty=psDefaultRowHeight InitialValue="minmax(var(--ft-row, 33px), max-content)" }
{ OverrideProperty=psCSSClass InitialValue="FtHost" }
Class cFTGridHost is a cFTLocalWebControlHost
    Procedure Construct_Object
        Forward Send Construct_Object

        Set peLayoutType to ltGrid
        Set psDefaultColumnWidth to "8px"
        Set psDefaultRowHeight to "minmax(var(--ft-row, 33px), max-content)"
    End_Procedure
End_Class
